{"text": "Kowalski, Karen\n\nFrom: Chambers, Kevin\nSent: Wednesday, March 18, 2015 2:08 PM\nTo: Kowalski, Karen\nSubject: RE: 2014-15 MBR\n\nAll the districts that filed are meeting their MBR. Bridgeport is not meeting their MBR stiff and | have to contact\nWillington. They were promised the money but my understanding is that they had to wait for a town meeting to allocate\n\nthe funds. | will contact you.\n\nKevin Chambers\nEducation Consultant\nState Department of Education\nBureau of Grants Management\n860-713-6455\n\nFrom: Kowalski, Karen\nSent: Wednesday, March 18, 2015 1:11 PM\nTo: Chambers, Kevin\nSubject: RE: 2014-15 MBR\n\nYEAH IIT!\n\nKaren Kowalski\nAssistant to the Chief Financial Officer\nFinance and Internal Operations Office\nConnecticut State Department of Education\n860-713-6451\n\nKaren.kowalski@ct.gov\n\nFrom: Chambers, Kevin\nSent: Wednesday, March 18, 2015 12:40 PM\nTo: Kowalski, Karen\nCc: Demsey, Kathleen\nSubject: 2014-15 MBR\n\nIt looks like all districts have filed and certified their 2014-15 ED012 form. | will run later to verify complaiance.\n\nKevin Chambers\nEducation Consultant\nState Department of Education\nBureau of Grants Management\n860-713-6455",
